import{_ as e,o as l,c as o,ao as a}from"./chunks/framework.Coh5k8j3.js";const w=JSON.parse('{"title":"Compatibility","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"compatibility/overview.md","filePath":"compatibility/overview.md","lastUpdated":null}'),d={name:"compatibility/overview.md"};function i(r,t,s,n,c,g){return l(),o("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[a('<h1 id="Compatibility" tabindex="-1">Compatibility <a class="header-anchor" href="#Compatibility" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Compatibility {#Compatibility}&quot;">​</a></h1><p>This section says, for each way of building a flow, which <strong>state types</strong>, <strong>element types</strong> and <strong>call styles</strong> work. Each page has a table and a minimal executable example for every cell.</p><div class="tip custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">How these pages stay true</p><ul><li><p><strong>Results are executed.</strong> Every ✓ / ⚠ / ✗ example is an <code>@example</code> block re-run on each documentation build, so a result cannot drift from the code.</p></li><li><p><strong>Scope comes from a probe.</strong> Which containers and axes are tested follows the CPU capability probe, <a href="https://github.com/control-toolbox/CTFlows.jl/blob/main/probe/cpu/probe_cpu.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><code>probe/cpu/probe_cpu.jl</code></a>. A new axis appears here once it is added to the probe.</p></li><li><p><strong>GPU is the exception.</strong> The documentation build has no device: the <a href="./gpu">GPU</a> page reports a run of <a href="https://github.com/control-toolbox/CTFlows.jl/tree/main/probe/gpu" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><code>probe/gpu</code></a>, not executed examples.</p></li></ul></div><h2 id="Pages" tabindex="-1">Pages <a class="header-anchor" href="#Pages" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Pages {#Pages}&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:right;">Constructor</th><th style="text-align:right;">Builds</th><th style="text-align:right;">Page</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><em>(all constructors)</em></td><td style="text-align:right;">—</td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="./shape_contract">Shape contract</a>: when a 1-D state is a scalar</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(::VectorField)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="/CTFlows.jl/stable/api/flows#CTFlows.Flows.StateFlow"><code>StateFlow</code></a></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="./vector_field"><code>Flow(VectorField)</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(::HamiltonianVectorField)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="/CTFlows.jl/stable/api/flows#CTFlows.Flows.HamiltonianFlow"><code>HamiltonianFlow</code></a></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="./hamiltonian_vector_field"><code>Flow(HamiltonianVectorField)</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(::Hamiltonian)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="/CTFlows.jl/stable/api/flows#CTFlows.Flows.HamiltonianFlow"><code>HamiltonianFlow</code></a></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="./hamiltonian"><code>Flow(Hamiltonian)</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(::ODEFunction)</code> / <code>Flow(::ODEProblem)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="/CTFlows.jl/stable/api/flows#CTFlows.Flows.StateFlow"><code>StateFlow</code></a> / <code>SciMLProblemFlow</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="./sciml"><code>Flow(SciML)</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(ocp)</code> (control-free)</td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="/CTFlows.jl/stable/api/flows#CTFlows.Flows.OptimalControlFlow"><code>OptimalControlFlow</code></a></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="./ocp_free"><code>Flow(ocp)</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(ocp, law)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="/CTFlows.jl/stable/api/flows#CTFlows.Flows.OptimalControlFlow"><code>OptimalControlFlow</code></a> / <a href="/CTFlows.jl/stable/api/flows#CTFlows.Flows.ControlledFlow"><code>ControlledFlow</code></a></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="./ocp_control_laws"><code>Flow(ocp, law)</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(h̃, law)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="/CTFlows.jl/stable/api/flows#CTFlows.Flows.HamiltonianFlow"><code>HamiltonianFlow</code></a></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="./pseudo_hamiltonian"><code>Flow(h̃, law)</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(h̃vf, law)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="/CTFlows.jl/stable/api/flows#CTFlows.Flows.HamiltonianFlow"><code>HamiltonianFlow</code></a></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="./pseudo_hamiltonian_vector_field"><code>Flow(h̃vf, law)</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(fc, law)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="/CTFlows.jl/stable/api/flows#CTFlows.Flows.ControlledFlow"><code>ControlledFlow</code></a></td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="./controlled_vector_field"><code>Flow(fc, law)</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><em>(all, on device)</em></td><td style="text-align:right;">—</td><td style="text-align:right;"><a href="./gpu">GPU</a></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="At-a-glance" tabindex="-1">At a glance <a class="header-anchor" href="#At-a-glance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;At a glance {#At-a-glance}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>&quot;Containers&quot; are scalars, <code>Vector</code>, <code>Matrix</code> (one column per trajectory), <code>MVector</code> / <code>SVector</code> and <code>MMatrix</code> / <code>SMatrix</code>. &quot;Real&quot; means <code>Float64</code> elements.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:right;">Constructor</th><th style="text-align:right;">Real, every container</th><th style="text-align:right;"><code>Complex</code></th><th style="text-align:right;">Hand-built <code>ForwardDiff.Dual</code></th><th style="text-align:right;">Caveat</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(VectorField)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">in-place field + immutable state: works, warns</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(HamiltonianVectorField)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">same as above</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(Hamiltonian)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✗</td><td style="text-align:right;">✗</td><td style="text-align:right;">AD-backed: differentiate the call, not a <code>Dual</code> state</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(::ODEFunction)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">same as <code>Flow(VectorField)</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(::ODEProblem)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">no shape coercion; in-place problem + immutable state: SciML error</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(ocp)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✗</td><td style="text-align:right;">✗</td><td style="text-align:right;">the state dimension is fixed by the OCP</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(ocp, DynClosedLoop)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✗</td><td style="text-align:right;">✗</td><td style="text-align:right;">same with <code>constraint=</code>/<code>multiplier=</code>; <code>:total</code> = <code>:partial</code> for a stationary law</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(ocp, OpenLoop/ClosedLoop)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">point call only</td><td style="text-align:right;">the trajectory call computes the objective, which is not <code>Dual</code>-transparent</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(h̃, law)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✗</td><td style="text-align:right;">✗</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>DynClosedLoop</code> only</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(h̃vf, law)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>DynClosedLoop</code> only; in-place + immutable: warns</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:right;"><code>Flow(fc, law)</code></td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;">✓</td><td style="text-align:right;"><code>OpenLoop</code>/<code>ClosedLoop</code> only</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Why the AD-backed flows reject <code>Complex</code> and hand-built <code>Dual</code> states: the default backend, <code>AutoForwardDiff</code>, does not handle <code>Complex</code>, and a <code>Dual</code> passed as <code>x0</code> collides with the flow&#39;s own <code>Dual</code>s. To get sensitivities of such a flow, wrap the <strong>call</strong> in <code>ForwardDiff.jacobian</code>; see <a href="./hamiltonian"><code>Flow(Hamiltonian)</code></a>.</p><p>On device, AD-free flows need no keyword: pass <code>CuArray</code>s. For AD-backed flows, <code>AutoMooncake</code> is the backend that handles every measured call shape; see <a href="./gpu">GPU</a>. On CPU, <code>AutoMooncake</code> works on every AD-backed flow too and pays off for large states; it refuses <code>Dual</code> states, i.e. an outer ForwardDiff through the flow.</p><h2 id="See-also" tabindex="-1">See also <a class="header-anchor" href="#See-also" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;See also {#See-also}&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><a href="./../flows/overview">Flows overview</a>: the data → systems → flows → trajectories pipeline.</p></li><li><p><a href="./../flows/building_a_flow">Building a flow</a>: the shortcut constructor and the explicit pipeline.</p></li><li><p><a href="./../flows/integrating">Integrating</a>: call styles, variable parameters, integrator options.</p></li></ul>',12)])])}const p=e(d,[["render",i]]);export{w as __pageData,p as default};
